Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-7" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:AllocatedShareBasedCompensationExpense" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="3" id="f-471">12,604</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cff0fc;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/></tr></table></div></ix:nonNumeric><div style="margin-bottom:12pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Determining the appropriate fair value model to measure the fair value of the stock option grants on the date of grant and the related assumptions requires judgment. <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfShareBasedPaymentAwardStockOptionsValuationAssumptionsTableTextBlock" id="f-472" continuedAt="f-472-1" escape="true">The fair value of each stock option grant is estimated using a Black-Scholes option-pricing model on the date of grant using the following inputs:</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><ix:continuation id="f-472-1"><div style="margin-bottom:12pt"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:71.930%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.081%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.406%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.083%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="9" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Years Ended December 31,</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f